 {en:"Lost in a New City",ar:"تائه في مدينة جديدة",v:"street sign|لافتة شارع|🪧;corner|زاوية|📐;straight|مستقيم|⬆️;turn|ينعطف|↪️;local|من أهل المكان|🧑;tourist|سائح|📸",
  c:[["Excuse me, how do I get to the museum?","Go straight and turn left at the corner.","Go straight and turn into a sandwich.","Museum is getting me."],["Have you been here before?","No, this is my first time in this city.","No, this is my first time in this soup.","Here has been me."],["Is it far from here?","No, it's only a five-minute walk.","No, it's only a five-minute cake.","Far is from here it."],["Could you show me on my phone?","Of course, it's right here, next to the park.","Of course, it's right here, next to Jupiter.","Phone is showing me could."]],
  l:"Sami and his father were lost in Istanbul. They had walked for an hour, but they couldn't find their hotel. A kind shop owner showed them the way on a map. The hotel was just around the corner.",
  lq:[["Where were Sami and his father?","in Istanbul","in Riyadh","in London"],["Who helped them?","a kind shop owner","a police officer","a taxi driver"],["Where was the hotel?","just around the corner","on the other side of the city","next to the airport"]],
  r:"Getting lost in a new city can be frightening, but it can also be an adventure. Before you go out, it is a good idea to write the name and address of your hotel on a card. If your phone stops working, you can show the card to a taxi driver. Try to remember big landmarks, such as a tall tower or a mosque. If you need help, ask a shop owner or a police officer rather than a stranger in the street. Most people are happy to help a polite visitor.",
  rq:[["What should you write on a card?","the name and address of your hotel","your favorite food","a joke"],["What should you try to remember?","big landmarks","every shop","the colors of cars"],["Who should you ask for help?","a shop owner or a police officer","any stranger","nobody"]]},
 {en:"The Map",ar:"الخريطة",v:"map|خريطة|🗺️;compass|بوصلة|🧭;route|مسار|〰️;symbol|رمز|🔣;mountain|جبل|⛰️;river|نهر|🏞️",
  c:[["What does this symbol on the map mean?","It shows where the mosque is.","It shows where the moon cake is.","Symbol is meaning me."],["Which route is shorter?","The road along the river is shorter.","The road along the cake is shorter.","Shorter is route the."],["Have you ever used a compass?","Yes, my scout leader taught me.","Yes, my sandwich taught me.","Compass has used me."],["Why do maps have a key?","To explain what the symbols mean.","To open the door of the map.","Key is a map why."]],
  l:"Before the hike, the scout leader gave everyone a map. He showed them how to use the key to understand the symbols. Blue lines are rivers, and brown lines show the mountains.",
  lq:[["Who gave everyone a map?","the scout leader","the teacher","the driver"],["What do blue lines show?","rivers","roads","mountains"],["What do brown lines show?","mountains","rivers","houses"]],
  r:"People have been making maps for thousands of years. One of the most famous mapmakers in history was Al-Idrisi, who lived about nine hundred years ago. He travelled widely and collected information from sailors and traders. Then he made a world map that was the most accurate of its time. It was so good that people used it for three hundred years. Today, we use maps on our phones, but they still depend on the same ideas: scale, symbols and direction.",
  rq:[["Who was Al-Idrisi?","a famous mapmaker","a pilot","a king"],["Where did he collect information from?","sailors and traders","books only","his dreams"],["How long did people use his map?","for three hundred years","for three years","for one week"]]},
 {en:"A Letter Home",ar:"رسالة إلى البيت",v:"letter|رسالة|✉️;stamp|طابع بريد|📮;address|عنوان|🏠;postcard|بطاقة بريدية|🖼️;miss|يشتاق|🥺;write|يكتب|✍️",
  c:[["Have you written to your grandmother yet?","Yes, I've just finished the letter.","Yes, I have write it tomorrow.","Grandmother has written me."],["What did you write about?","I wrote about our trip to the mountains.","I wrote about a purple Thursday.","Write has about me."],["Do you miss home?","Yes, I miss my family very much.","Yes, I miss my family's fridge very much.","Home is missing me."],["Where should I put the stamp?","Put it in the top right corner.","Put it inside your shoe.","Stamp is putting where."]],
  l:"Dear Grandma, we have been in Abha for three days. The weather is cool, and we have walked in the green mountains every day. I have bought you a small present. I miss you. Love, Reem.",
  lq:[["Where is Reem?","in Abha","in Jeddah","in Dubai"],["How is the weather?","cool","very hot","stormy"],["What has Reem bought?","a small present","a big bag","a new phone"]],
  r:"Before phones and email, letters were the main way to send news to family far away. A letter could take weeks to arrive, so people wrote long, careful messages. Many families still keep old letters in boxes, and reading them is like opening a window to the past. Today, writing a letter by hand has become rare, which makes it even more special. A handwritten card shows that you have taken time to think about someone. Why not write one this week to a person you love?",
  rq:[["How long could a letter take to arrive?","weeks","seconds","one hour"],["What is reading old letters like?","opening a window to the past","watching a film","eating a meal"],["Why is a handwritten card special?","It shows you have taken time to think about someone.","It is cheap.","It is fast."]]},
 {en:"Coming Back",ar:"العودة",v:"unpack|يفرغ الحقيبة|🧳;souvenir|تذكار|🎁;tired|متعب|🥱;welcome|ترحيب|🤗;home|بيت|🏡;photos|صور|📸",
  c:[["Welcome back! How was your trip?","It was amazing, but I've missed home.","It was amazing, but I've missed the moon.","Trip has welcomed me."],["Have you unpacked your suitcase?","Not yet, I'm too tired.","Not yet, I'm too purple.","Suitcase unpacked me has."],["Did you bring any souvenirs?","Yes, I've brought a small gift for everyone.","Yes, I've brought a small cloud for everyone.","Souvenir bring did."],["What was the best part?","Seeing the old castle on the hill.","Seeing my own shoes.","Part was best."]],
  l:"After two weeks in Malaysia, the Al-Otaibi family has come home. The children are tired but happy. They have brought souvenirs for their cousins. Tonight, everyone is coming to see the photos.",
  lq:[["Where has the family been?","Malaysia","Egypt","Turkey"],["How long were they away?","two weeks","two days","two months"],["What is happening tonight?","Everyone is coming to see the photos.","They are flying again.","They are going to sleep early."]],
  r:"Coming home after a long journey is a special feeling. Your own bed feels softer, and the food tastes better than anywhere else. Many travellers say that a trip helps them see their home with new eyes. They notice things they had never noticed before, like the friendly neighbours or the beautiful sunset over the city. Unpacking can be boring, but it is also a chance to remember every moment of the journey. Some families make a photo book together so they can enjoy the memories for years.",
  rq:[["How does your own bed feel?","softer","harder","colder"],["What does a trip help travellers do?","see their home with new eyes","forget their home","sleep more"],["What do some families make together?","a photo book","a new suitcase","a cake"]]}
